            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 0.8 (build 593)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Voice notes come up to a normal level.</b> If your Mac's microphone records quietly, a voice note is leveled automatically when you stop: the speech is brought up to a standard volume before it is transcribed or shared, with peaks kept clean. A recording that was already fine is left exactly as it was, and a note with nobody speaking stays quiet rather than becoming hiss.</li>
<li><b>Color settings fixes.</b> The input color space list now scrolls on its own and the Filter field works. A new "Views listed in the menu" section lets you prune which views the View menu offers, the same way displays are pruned.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
